  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Assistance to victims of severe weather conditions, Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is an emergency response to continuing severe climatic conditions affecting Colombia (including heavy rains, flooding, gales, and hail). An estimated 751,744 people have been affected up to 5th November 2007. This project will meet the needs of 1,200 families (SNPS are assuming there are 5 people per family = 6,000 people) in the following areas of the Caribbean region in the departments of Atl&#xE1;ntico, Magdalena, Bol&#xED;var, C&#xF3;rdoba and Guajira. The Project will last for 6 months (5 months for project activities, 1 month for reporting) and will focus on Caribbean region in the departments of Atl&#xE1;ntico, Magdalena, Bol&#xED;var, C&#xF3;rdoba and Guajira. The total SOA appeals for &#xA3;106,015.82 (equivalent of 438,350,000 Colombian pesos using CAFOD exchange rate for November 2007 where &#xA3;1 = 4,134.76).</narrative>
  </description>
